From 9fc3fce2ba3a24c18ba77a58f10f5c617e600b74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:50:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(checkpoints): reclaim with auto_prune off, niced long gc,
 daily stuck-over-cap ERROR [daveey]

Follows 7dfcf91c967 (take path touches only its own project and defers the gc). What
that leaves: only the periodic prune frees space, and on the MacBook it never did.

- auto_prune: false turned off the size cap too: with no periodic run the deferred gc
  (.gc-pending) never happened and the store sat at 15 GB against a 500 MB cap. A pending
  gc now gets a size-only run (retention_days=0, never deletes a project) at most once
  per min_interval_hours.
- Pruner(maintenance=True) (periodic prune + `hermes checkpoints prune`) runs its gc
  under `nice -n 10` with MAINTENANCE_GC_TIMEOUT (1800 s) instead of 3x the
  tool timeout: 90 s killed a 14 GB gc in its prune phase on every run.
- enforce_size gcs after 1, 2, 4, ... rewrites instead of after every rewrite: with a gc
  that now completes (minutes on a GB store), one per rewrite over ~800 projects would
  hold the store lock, and skip every checkpoint, for hours. At most 2x the needed drops.
- check_store_health: once a day, ERROR `checkpoint store over cap: X GB / Y MB, last
  prune Z` when the store is over 2x its cap and no prune ran for 48 h (or ever), so the
  self-heal lane files it. The size walk is gated by its daily marker.

Tests (test_checkpoint_size_pending.py): 7 of 9 fail on 7dfcf91c967 (auto_prune-off
prune skipped; no health check; maintenance reclaim killed at 3x timeout; no nice;
151 gcs for 150 drops).
Self-heal agent-23a0c3b69f.
